{"title":"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perimeter of an equilateral triangle exceeds the perimeter of a square by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73c661e8a0d799ddb6253a40d38e4761e7f285c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1989 \\ \\text{cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />. The length of each side of the triangle exceeds the length of each side of the square by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49a9727094809c4c74405eebe53c8b7b83dab23d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d \\ \\text{cm}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" />. The square has perimeter greater than 0. How many positive integers are NOT possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c10c58d7db37ba859060aee6ccc72b9e6890f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} \\ 0 \\qquad \\text{(B)} \\ 9 \\qquad \\text{(C)} \\ 221 \\qquad \\text{(D)} \\ 663 \\qquad \\text{(E)} \\ \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of the square.  Then the triangle has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/5/b7538110e7fe729aa790c222209cd179b467d9f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, and the difference of their perimeters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a48a82a5a0d11ad3465e33536a022d30524b16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(s + d) - 4s = 3d - s = 1989$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" />.  \n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e502aa058c2862adcaa629ba3fe38ba31b748d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{s + 1989}{3} = \\frac{s}{3} + 663$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"193\" height=\"38\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35a1327f60f1440b02baa16dc350b245dfb4515b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/5695a557bdcd07f639a4adb3f0bf7214eda7f4ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d &gt; 663$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> and thus the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c59af2af4d76d1fddebabaac4b7b5fcdd1f5d17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$663$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> positive integers are not possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152cb6db55528ec8f8f962ebb2860d05933aac5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 664$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> is a possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca06559a7cce61e20489336085fb507d7aa7e41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 3(n - 663)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" /> would suffice.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f07c71673338a34243fb869ecd4f4ebb0bb17dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 663}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" /> positive integers are not possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME\" title=\"1989 AHSME\">1989 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1989 AHSME Problems/Problem